Track 3: Sister Helen Misses Her Train
- Story & Context: Now a legendary piece of Liturgic-Wave folklore, this final track mythologizes a runaway novice nun who fled the abbey with a suitcase full of transcribed dream patches, only to get stranded at a deserted Normandy railway station. Built around a mesmerizing, motorik flute arpeggio that mimics the rhythm of a idling locomotive, the track slowly dissolves into an ocean of psychedelic phase-shifting and chant-like woodwind harmonics. The recording ends with the real ambient sound of a distant train whistle echoing over a decaying synth chord. A haunting, multi-tracked vocal chorus gently repeats, "The platform ticket melted in her hand."
